# Verify — etude-9uf.1: `etude gate`

## The contract, item by item, against the built binary

The supervisor runbook obliges this bead's verify phase to walk its ten-item
contract against the real binary rather than against tests. Done below with
`./bin/etude` built from this tree.

| # | Contract item | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Unknown stage → clear error, non-zero, nothing recorded | `unknown stage "bogus" in .etude/workflow.yaml; stages are: plan, implement, verify, docs, review` — exit 1; run ref gate count unchanged |
| 2 | Reads the stage's `gate.tier`/`abstraction`/`checks` | the live `plan` gate resolved tier L2 and inlined the plan stage's abstraction into the prompt (asserted byte-for-byte by `TestGateStagePassRecordsOneAttemptAndAdvances`) |
| 3 | Resolves the tier's seats from `registry.yaml`; no flag can lighten it | there is no seat/tier flag on the command; `--help` shows only `--run/--stage/--artifact/--workflow/--timeout` |
| 4 | Missing run ref → clear error, non-zero | `run not found: refs/etude/runs/absent-run; capture the stage first (etude capture <stage> --run absent-run ...)` — exit 1 |
| 5 | Derives the round from attempts already on the run | live: successive real invocations recorded `plan.r3`, `plan.r4`, then `implement.r2` without being told a round |
| 6 | Runs checks then seats against the same shared prompt | `TestGateStagePassRecordsOneAttemptAndAdvances` asserts both seats received byte-identical input |
| 7 | Fail-closed synthesis | live `implement.r2`: one `go`, one `failed` → `escalated`, not a pass |
| 8 | Appends one `GateAttempt` with per-seat verdicts, raw output, session evidence | `etude run show etude-9uf.1` lists every attempt with seat verdicts; `TestGateStageRecordParitesWithCaptureGate` asserts session-evidence and raw-output fields |
| 9 | Prints the verdict and each blocking seat's `required` | live output shows `gate implement.r2: escalated` then per-seat lines with notes |
| 10 | Exit 0 only on pass | unknown stage / missing run / no reviewable stage / missing flags all exit 1; a not-passing gate exits 1 while still recording the attempt |

Additional guards exercised live: an empty artifact is refused
(`artifact /tmp/e.md is empty; there is nothing to review`), and a run that
exists but has no stage producing the phase's role is refused
(`no reviewable stage on run: ... capture it before gating stage "verify"`),
which is what enforces capture-before-gate per phase rather than merely
"the run exists".

